// Detector 1 of 4: step changes — sudden jumps in cost.
// Catches resize-and-forget and incidents.
//
// Design choices, each suppressing a specific false positive:
//   Weekly not daily  — nonprod VMs run at 14% on weekends; a daily
//                       comparison would flag every Monday on every dev box.
//   serialize + prev()— KQL has no window functions. The ResourceName guard
//                       stops comparing across resource boundaries.
//   PrevWeek > 5      — $0.02 -> $0.20 is +900% and worth nothing. Percentage
//                       change needs an absolute floor underneath it.
//
// Result at threshold 75%: 4 rows — 2 true positives (dev VM resize 2026-03-12,
// logging incident 2026-04-06), 1 duplicate (same incident, partial week then
// full week), 1 false positive (holiday freeze ending, dev activity resuming).
// 50% precision. Raising to 150% gives 100% precision but goes blind to any
// real problem growing slower than that. Neither threshold is "right".

AzureBilling_CL
| extend D = todatetime(Date)
| extend Week = startofweek(D)
| where Week > datetime(2025-09-07) and Week < datetime(2026-08-16)
| summarize WeeklyCost = sum(CostInBillingCurrency) by ResourceName, Week
| order by ResourceName asc, Week asc
| serialize
| extend PrevWeek = iff(prev(ResourceName) == ResourceName, prev(WeeklyCost), real(null))
| where isnotnull(PrevWeek) and PrevWeek > 5
| extend PctChange = round(100.0 * (WeeklyCost - PrevWeek) / PrevWeek, 1)
| where PctChange > 75
| project Week, ResourceName, PrevWeek = round(PrevWeek, 2), WeeklyCost = round(WeeklyCost, 2), PctChange
| order by PctChange desc
